{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## /rebar-debug — fix landed for review (Gerrit change 2428)\n\n**Re-verified on current origin/main** (`1876ed4a4c1f`, which includes changes 2421 + 2426 to\n`autodeploy.sh`). The defect stands exactly as the RCA describes; only line numbers moved:\n\n- `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:179` — `SECRETS_PATHS='infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh infra/terraform/ssm.tf'`\n- `:853-854` — the **review-bot** gate ORs it: `changed_range \"$bot_deployed\" \"$TARGET\" \"$BOT_PATHS\" || changed_range \"$bot_deployed\" \"$TARGET\" \"$SECRETS_PATHS\"` ✅ (the standing-intent precedent, f600 / incident 2731).\n- `:872` and `:876` (pre-fix) — the **mcp** gate did NOT, on either the backoff-active or backoff-clear arm: `changed_range \"$mcp_deployed\" \"$TARGET\" \"$MCP_PATHS\"` ❌.\n\n**RED proof (mechanism, not a source read).** Added `test_secrets_only_change_redeploys_mcp` to\nthe shipped-script real-bash harness (`tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py::_real_git_box`),\nparametrized over `infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh` and `infra/terraform/ssm.tf` (added `ssm.tf` to\nthe harness baseline). Pre-fix, a secrets-only target commit produced:\n\n```\ncmds=['tag compose-review-bot:latest compose-review-bot:prev','compose-build-review-bot','compose-up-review-bot']\njournal: \"review-bot sources or secrets changed; ... rebuild + restart\"\njournal: \"deploy complete: env now reflects <target>\"\n```\n\nNo `compose-build-mcp`, no `run --name rebar-mcp-…` — the tick reports **complete** and stamps\nthe target sha, so the delta is consumed and never retried. Both parametrizations RED on the\n`compose-build-mcp` assertion for the right reason. The test asserts BOTH the rebuild AND a new\nmcp container start (refreshing files on disk without a new container is the non-fix).\n\n**Fix.** Added an `mcp_delta()` helper beside `changed()` that returns true when EITHER `MCP_PATHS`\nor `SECRETS_PATHS` changed over `$mcp_deployed..$TARGET`; called from BOTH mcp gate arms. Mirrors\nthe review-bot gate exactly. Post-fix both parametrizations GREEN; a defect-seeded mutation\n(re-omitting `SECRETS_PATHS`) returns the test to RED, confirming teeth (run under `sandbox-exec`).\nFull module: 44 passed. `make lint` + `make typecheck` clean.\n\n**Attribution — `caused_by` = `6964-40bb-46c9-48a7` (panicky-sylphish-foxterrier), class `plan_defect`.**\n`SECRETS_PATHS` was introduced by `820159375abd` (f600, 2026-07-20). The MCP gate + `MCP_PATHS`\nwere added five weeks later by `2a0a4b19f2ab` (`rebar-ticket: 6964-40bb-46c9-48a7`,\n\"infra: add mcp blue-green autodeploy target\"; `git log -S'MCP_PATHS=' -- infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`).\nThis is the missed-consumer-update case: the new mcp component consumed fetch-secrets output but\nits delta gate was planned against `MCP_PATHS` alone — the obligation predated the consumer, so\nattribution goes to the ticket that ADDED the gate, not to f600 (which created the obligation and\ncould not have known about a component that did not yet exist). A whole-file blame majority on\n`autodeploy.sh` would name neither, so this divergence is recorded per protocol.\n\n**Step 7 parity sweep.** Rule: *a component whose delta gate decides redeploy AND consumes\nfetch-secrets output must OR `SECRETS_PATHS`.* Census of autodeploy delta gates: review-bot\n(BOT_PATHS — has it ✅), mcp (MCP_PATHS — was the MISSING slot, now fixed ✅), certbot/obs/config\ngates (do NOT consume fetch-secrets `.env` — N/A). No other siblings; construct sweep also finds\nonly the mcp site.\n\n**Scope out of scope (AC3).** A pure SSM VALUE rotation advances no git ref, so no git-delta gate\ncan observe it — by construction, not omission. That path stays operator-driven via\n`infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md`; this fix does not and cannot replace it.\n\n**AC4 (live validation) — DEFERRED TO DEPLOY WINDOW.** Authored under a read-only-box constraint.\nAC4 requires observing a real secrets-only deploy on the box (autodeploy journal lines + the new\nmcp container identity carrying the refreshed value). That cannot be done from this change and\nmust be recorded by an operator at the next secrets-only deploy. The code fix + its test land now;\nAC4 remains open for live verification.\n\nGerrit: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2428 — awaiting `LLM-Review +1` and\n`Verified +1` before Submit + close."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788085636912796606,"uuid":"26b4f698-2fc1-4d4a-a211-fb86b41cceb5"}